    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Runtime and persistence boundary",
      "items": [
        "kind is a single-workstation, one-control-plane Kubernetes lab; it is not EKS, Multi-AZ or a cloud deployment.",
        "Calico enforces default-deny ingress/egress with explicit DNS, database, scrape and OTLP paths.",
        "PostgreSQL has one 1Gi PVC, not HA or RDS. Tempo/Prometheus local retention is bounded; recovery evidence is not cloud DR."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Scope and source evidence",
      "items": [
        "The arrows show requests, writes, scrapes and trace export; Grafana query arrows name destination ports.",
        "Argo CD application ownership, direct Helm alternative, CI and offline infrastructure validation are in the delivery view.",
        "Compose also offers a separate API/PostgreSQL development profile; no connection to the planned AWS graph exists."
      ]
    }
